Description: Rewrite Ghostty 1.4 CSS for GTK 4.14 / libadwaita 1.5 (Ubuntu 24.04)
 Ghostty 1.4.0's CSS uses syntax added in GTK 4.16 and libadwaita 1.6:
 color-mix(), var(--...) custom properties, relative oklab() colors,
 space-separated hsl() and gradient color hints. GTK 4.14 drops each rule
 it can't parse and logs "Theme parser error" or "css parsing failed" at
 startup. The affected elements (child-exited banner, error progress bar, bell overlay, drop
 zones, split divider, read-only overlay text, window-theme=ghostty
 headerbar) fall back to default theme colors.
 .
 This patch rewrites those rules, in style.css and in the runtime CSS
 generated by application.zig, using the libadwaita 1.5 named colors:
 .
   color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-color), transparent 50%)
     -> alpha(@accent_color, 0.5)
   :root { --window-bg-color: var(--ghostty-bg); }
     -> @define-color window_bg_color @ghostty_bg;
   oklab(from var(--headerbar-bg-color) calc(l * 0.9) a b / alpha)
     -> shade(@ghostty_bg, 0.9)
   linear-gradient(to left, transparent, 50%, X 50%)
     -> linear-gradient(to left, transparent 50%, X 50%)
 .
 Release tarballs ship style.css precompiled into
 src/apprt/gtk/ghostty_resources.c, so the Dockerfile runs
 patches/repack-gresource.sh after this patch to put the patched
 stylesheet into that bundle.
 .
 libadwaita 1.5 has no overview_* colors, so the tab overview keeps its
 default colors with window-theme=ghostty.
 .
 Applies after 01-gtk-4.14-build.patch. Written against Ghostty 1.4.0. If
 a newer release fails to apply it, check the new CSS for syntax GTK 4.14
 doesn't support (look for "Theme parser error" or "css parsing failed" in
 the smoke test log).
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-27
